ACMCoder integration changes (2026), relative to the fixed upstream
wasm-clang-runtime revision df1180d80184733c6a01599f76b92b4001d20f87:
- clang22 and lld22 WASM: added 512 MiB linear-memory maximums.
- memfs WASM: rebuilt using wasi-sdk 33 and added a 128 MiB
  linear-memory maximum.
- sysroot archive: replaced its iostream header with the wasi-sdk 33
  noeh header from LLVM revision 4434dabb69916856b824f68a64b029c67175e532.
- generated worker.js: adapted upstream shared.js method binding and
  virtual-file allocation limits, then appended ACMCoder's worker bridge.
- runtime files are gzip-compressed for distribution.

The source scripts and fixed-resource provenance are in the ACMCoder
source release: scripts/bundle-cpp.mjs, scripts/wasm-memory-limit.mjs,
shared/runners/cpp-worker.js, third_party/cpp/README.md and
experiments/browser-languages/prepare.py.
